<td id="S4.F8.3.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.4pt;padding-right:1.4pt;"><img src="2603.10785v1/figs/ShowLine-Image4-SOTA-30.jpg" id="S4.F8.g27" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:79/79;" width="79" height="79" alt="Refer to caption"></td>
<td id="S4.F8.3.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.4pt;padding-right:1.4pt;"><img src="2603.10785v1/figs/ShowLine-Image4-SOTA-45.jpg" id="S4.F8.g28" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:79/79;" width="79" height="79" alt="Refer to caption"></td>
<td id="S4.F8.3.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.4pt;padding-right:1.4pt;"><img src="2603.10785v1/figs/ShowLine-Image4-SGA-30.jpg" id="S4.F8.g29" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:79/79;" width="79" height="79" alt="Refer to caption"></td>
<td id="S4.F8.3.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.4pt;padding-right:1.4pt;"><img src="2603.10785v1/figs/ShowLine-Image4-SGA-45.jpg" id="S4.F8.g30" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:79/79;" width="79" height="79" alt="Refer to caption"></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F8.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="S4.F8.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:113%;">Qualitative Comparison (Cross-Architecture).<span id="S4.F8.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Domains <math id="S4.F8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S4.F8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, evaluated on both SDXL and FLUX. Reference images (left) define each target domain.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Evaluation Protocol</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each dataset, we generate outputs from four variants—Baseline and SGA at <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>—using 8 domain-specific prompts with <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math>5 seeds each, yielding <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math>40 samples per variant.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Primary Metrics: Perceptual Evaluation.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both evaluator types rank the four outputs from lowest to highest quality:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Judge:</span> Following the LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>, which has been extended to visual generation evaluation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, we employ GPT 5.2 with a specialized system prompt evaluating GDA fidelity across three dimensions: geometric and symbolic accuracy, rendering quality, and overall aesthetic coherence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human Evaluation:</span> Following established protocols for verifiable and reproducible perceptual assessment <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, we conduct blind user studies with 20 participants recruited via the Prolific platform and domain-specific communities.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We report <em id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">1st-place rate</em> and <em id="S4.SS3.SSSx1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">aggregate rank distribution</em> as primary metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Quantitative Results</h3>

<figure id="S4.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.10785v1/figure_eval_llm.svg" id="S4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/261;" width="476" height="261"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="S4.F9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative Evaluation — LLM Judge (GPT 5.2).<span id="S4.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Aggregate rank distribution (left) and per-dataset 1st-place rate heatmap (right). SGA variants achieve favourable rankings across both architectures and all stylistic domains.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.10785v1/figure_eval_human.svg" id="S4.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/260;" width="476" height="260"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="S4.F10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Quantitative Evaluation — Human Evaluation.<span id="S4.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Matching layout to <a href="#S4.F9" title="In 4.4 Quantitative Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ The Quadratic Geometry of Flow Matching: Semantic Granularity Alignment for Text-to-Image Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Human rankings corroborate the automated assessment, with SGA variants accumulating the majority of top rankings.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S4.F9" title="In 4.4 Quantitative Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ The Quadratic Geometry of Flow Matching: Semantic Granularity Alignment for Text-to-Image Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#S4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 4.4 Quantitative Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ The Quadratic Geometry of Flow Matching: Semantic Granularity Alignment for Text-to-Image Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, SGA variants achieve favourable rankings across both evaluator types and architectures. On FLUX, SGA (<math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>) achieves a 1st-place rate of 40% in the LLM Judge, while both baselines remain below 20%; human rankings corroborate this trend. The synchronized results across FLUX and Animagine XL 3.1 suggest architecture-independent effectiveness, with per-dataset heatmaps confirming consistency across domains.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Efficiency.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notably, SGA at <math id="S4.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> consistently outranks Baseline at <math id="S4.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in both LLM and human evaluations, indicating that SGA achieves superior quality with approximately 33% less training compute. This suggests that aligning semantic granularity enables more efficient manifold learning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Calibration Metrics.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We additionally report three embedding-based metrics: <span id="S4.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIP-I</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> (image–image similarity, domain fidelity), <span id="S4.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIP-T</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> (text–image similarity, prompt alignment), and <span id="S4.SS4.SSSx2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DINO-I</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> (structural correspondence). As shown in <a href="#S4.T1" title="In Calibration Metrics. ‣ 4.4 Quantitative Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ The Quadratic Geometry of Flow Matching: Semantic Granularity Alignment for Text-to-Image Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, SGA improves or maintains all metrics on both frameworks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Calibration Metrics<span id="S4.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (averaged across datasets). Higher is better for all metrics. <math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" mathcolor="#009900" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math> denotes improvement of SGA over the Baseline.</span></span></figcaption>
