<section id="Pt0.A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.F.2 </span>Per-Domain Training Budget</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As stated in the main text, training budgets are reported as multiples of a reference GPU-time: <math id="Pt0.A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the shorter checkpoint and <math id="Pt0.A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}=1.5\,N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}=1.5\,N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> the longer one. <a href="#Pt0.A6.T4" title="In 0.F.2 Per-Domain Training Budget ‣ Appendix 0.F Full Experimental Setup ‣ The Quadratic Geometry of Flow Matching: Semantic Granularity Alignment for Text-to-Image Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> lists the estimated wall-clock GPU hours for each domain on a single RTX PRO 6000.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Pt0.A6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A6.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Estimated GPU hours per domain (FLUX).<span id="Pt0.A6.T4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="Pt0.A6.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A6.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the two evaluation checkpoints. Actual models used for evaluation are the closest saved checkpoints to the listed times.</span></span></figcaption>
